sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2015-girardia-08> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "In canonical variate shape space, the D. japonica head morphology lies between those of G. dorotocephala and S. mediterranea, and octanol-induced S. mediterranea-like G. dorotocephala heads remodel by moving from S. mediterranea-like to D. japonica-like to G. dorotocephala morphology.";
    dc:type "experimental-result";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Head remodeling passes from S. mediterranea-like to D. japonica-like to normal shape";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Emmons-Bell M, Durant F, Hammelman J, Bessonov N, Volpert V, Morokuma J, Pinet K, Adams DS, Pietak A, Lobo D, Levin M, “Gap Junctional Blockade Stochastically Induces Different Species-Specific Head Anatomies in Genetically Wild-Type Girardia dorotocephala Flatworms”, International journal of molecular sciences (2015), doi:10.3390/ijms161126065; section “2. Results › 2.7. Induced Shape Changes Are Not Permanent”. Scope: Remodeling octanol-treated G. dorotocephala regenerates, days 10–30"
}
